 "intro_zh": "塔尔寺又名塔儿寺，创建于明洪武十年，是中国藏传佛教格鲁派（黄教）六大寺院之一，是中国西北地区藏传佛教的活动中心。酥油花、壁画和堆绣被誉为“塔尔寺艺术三绝”。寺内还珍藏了许多佛教典籍和历史、文学、哲学、医药、立法等方面的学术专著。塔尔寺每年举行的佛事活动“四大法会”，也是热闹非凡。",
 "intro_en": "Kumbum Temple, also known as Pagoda Temple, was founded in the 10th year of Hongwu in the Ming Dynasty. It is one of the six major monasteries of the Gelug Sect (Yellow Sect) of Tibetan Buddhism in China and the center of Tibetan Buddhism activities in northwest China. Butter flowers, murals and embroidery are known as the \"three unique arts of Kumbum Temple\". The temple also houses many Buddhist classics and academic monographs on history, literature, philosophy, medicine, legislation, etc. The annual Buddhist activities \"Four Dharma Assemblies\" held in Kumbum Monastery are also very lively.",
 "intro_en_source": "machine_translation",
